WEBVTT

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.850
Well, then. Farewell.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.480
Good night.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.190
My, he's a peculiar tengu.
Isn't he, Yasaburo?

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:12.930
Oh, Benten-sama...

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.630
Please, hold back your rage.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.000
I wouldn't say that I'm angry.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.620
Not over something this petty.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.610
Huh?

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.030
<b>Episode Four
The Tanuki Shogi Tournament</b>

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.230
What's most important is charm.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.530
<b>Okazaki Group</b>

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.910
But we're not looking for flattery.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.040
We take pride in playing
our roles as tanuki.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.390
That's the trick.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.170
Well, thanks for watching the place for us.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.610
The transformation technique
that we tanuki are so good at

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.760
cannot be used inside a cage.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.770
The transformation technique is strongly
connected to the idea of freedom.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:50.340
That's why we have always left the role

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:54.280
of playing captive tanuki at the zoo
to the Okazaki family,

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.030
professionals at playing the role
and trading places while playing it.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.780
That frog is driving that tanuki!

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.980
But you sure do dabble in a lot of things.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.840
You have nothing but respect from me.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.790
I don't really have anything else to do.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.170
Not to mention the pay for playing
the stand-in is quite good.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.910
Oh, right.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.050
You're playing in the shogi tournament.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.910
A bad bush is better than an open field.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.140
I mean, there aren't that many
tanuki that like shogi.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.060
I'd feel bad for the Nanzenjis if it
ended up a rather empty tournament.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.480
On that note, wasn't there a shogi room?

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.070
Oh, there was.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.530
Father's secret base, right?

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.700
That was a fun room.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.100
What's going on with that room now?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.410
It should be in the Tadasu Forest,

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.950
but I'm not sure myself.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.370
Yaichiro doesn't know
where the room is either?

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.200
Apparently not.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:58.930
It appears that Father hid it quite well.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.360
I'd like to go back there someday.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.720
You play a splendid tanuki, Yasaburo-chan.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.410
Gyokuran, what brings you here?

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:13.430
I heard that you were standing in
for the Okazaki family today,

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.310
so I thought I'd show my support.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.350
Oh, Yajiro-kun.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:19.440
Hey.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.480
You're participating in the
shogi tournament, right, Yajiro-kun?

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:23.500
Yeah.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:26.350
And you're coming to watch,
aren't you, Yasaburo-chan?

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:27.930
I'm not sure.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.910
I'm not really interested in shogi.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:34.330
Yaichiro-san worked so hard to bring it back,
but you're not coming?

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.790
You shouldn't be so cold.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.650
I'm sure it'll be fun if you come.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:43.010
Well, I'm sure it'll be fun
for you, Gyokuran.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:47.570
Yaichiro-san still isn't
playing shogi, is he?

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.410
Yeah.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.180
You know better than anyone else,
don't you, Gyokuran?

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.150
I wonder how long he'll let it bother him.

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:57.460
He's a fully grown furball now.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.360
Well, did you tell him that?

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.790
I can't.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.820
I'm not sure why, but I just can't.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.460
Well, I'll see you at the shogi tournament.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:16.610
Were it not for this
furry little love story...

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:18.500
What, Nii-san?

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.840
No, it's nothing.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.680
That was rather suggestive.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:26.860
Even frogs at the bottoms of wells
have to keep some things to themselves.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:33.740
Thank you all

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:38.520
for coming to the Nanzenji Tanuki
Shogi Tournament tonight.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:43.150
We hope that this tournament
will remain annual for years to come.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.780
I am Nanzenji Shojiro.
I will be your host this evening.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:52.610
From the west, we have Nanzenji Gyokuran.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.110
From the east, we have Shimogamo Yajiro.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.710
<b>Eastern Army</b>

00:05:58.960 --> 00:05:59.620
Whoo!

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:01.300
It's Beauty and the Frog!

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.440
Good evening, Yaichiro-san.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.970
Good evening, Gyokuran.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:13.010
It's all thanks to you that
this day came to pass, Yaichiro-san.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.490
You are too kind.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.310
I'm very relieved, as well.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:22.310
I'm not going to hold back, Yajiro-kun.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:30.160
Gyokuran's disappointed that you
didn't enter the tournament, Nii-san.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.570
I'm a nobody.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.740
Even if I entered,

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.490
I wouldn't be able to get
past the preliminaries.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:40.840
I'm nowhere near qualified enough
to play against Gyokuran.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.090
<b>Knight</b>

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.590
<b>Silver General</b>

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.590
<b>Gold General</b>

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.590
<b>King</b>

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.750
First move, Shimogamo Yajiro.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:52.090
7-6, pawn.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.850
<b>Pawn</b>

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.340
Second, Nanzenji Gyokuran.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.600
3-4, pawn.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.750
6-6, pawn.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.440
6-2, silver general.

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:17.870
This is not a mere pawn,
but one of the four ultimate kings,

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:21.620
the Fool Hermit who does as he pleases!

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:26.160
And over here, we have...

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.670
The sly old dog, the Pink Tanuki,

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:31.090
and the American Minister!

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:34.010
7-7, knight.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:36.640
You got it!

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.600
<b>Knight</b>

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.560
<b>Silver General</b>

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.480
You're being obnoxious, Ginkaku.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.860
Apparently, you don't recognize art
when you hear it.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:53.040
I am currently learning the ways
of an English gentleman.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.370
Playing the violin is a necessary skill.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.640
If you guys can become English gentlemen,

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.370
so could a shogoin daikon.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:02.850
What did you say?

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.120
Why, you brute!

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.680
Just ignore him!

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.790
There is honor in isolation!

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.880
Yes, honor in isolation!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.470
I'm pretty sure isolation without honor
just means you're a loner.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:15.680
Hush your mouth!

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.950
Just wait, Ginkaku.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:20.640
Your big brother's coming to save you!

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:22.300
Oh, pardon me.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.100
Don't go moving on your own!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:29.990
Honestly, tanuki like you
are always so ungentlemanly.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:33.360
<b>Silver General</b>

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:33.360
<b>Gold General</b>

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:33.360
<b>Knight</b>

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:33.360
Tanuki like him will never evolve, Nii-san.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.580
But we're different.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.400
We do nothing but evolve.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:41.930
We advance, and we grow.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:44.070
Better be on your guard.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:44.830
Got it?

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.380
<b>Prancing 
Stag</b>

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.380
<b>Drunken
 Elephant</b>

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.380
Like them apples?

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.510
There aren't any weird pieces like that.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:56.800
You are such an uneducated fellow.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.790
This is an actual piece that used
to be used in shogi a long time ago.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:05.100
Mediocre pawns don't suit
extraordinary men like us.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:09.690
Then I'll just have to be one
of the Ultimate Four Kings.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:13.360
<b>Fool Hermit</b>

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.360
The Fool Hermit!

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.870
There's no piece like that!

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.820
In that case...

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.640
Whoosh.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.160
<b>Gozu Tenno</b>

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.160
<b>Emperor</b>

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.160
Schwing!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.790
<b>American Minister</b>

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.380
<b>Throughout Heaven and Earth</b>

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:31.380
I'm in the groove.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.130
Same here.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.130
<b>Self-Righteous</b>

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.130
<b>King of All Cosmos</b>

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:37.840
That's enough, Yasaburo!

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:51.480
<b>Rook</b>

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:51.480
<b>Knight</b>

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.960
At least we're keeping
the battle on the board.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.920
This is a very important event
for the Nanzenjis.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:47.320
No messing around with those two idiots!

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.420
As if I'm going to back down now!

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:51.480
Are you trying to embarrass Gyokuran?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.940
Aha. I knew it.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.490
I always thought
you were suspicious, Yaichiro.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.950
What are you talking about?

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.660
I was thinking about how you're always
so kind to the Nanzeji family,

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:08.290
yet you're always so unkind to us.

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:11.300
You want to be the Trick Magister,

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:15.300
but don't you think it's unfair
if you keep favoring the Nanzenjis?

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.040
I mean, even with this shogi tournament,

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:21.050
you've been helping out quite a bit.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:25.990
We Ebisugawas offered you a drum
filled with Trick Denki Bran,

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:29.310
and we didn't even get
a single "thank you" for it.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.380
How could you treat us like that?

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.190
Just how unfortunate am I?

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.650
The way I see it,

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:40.200
the reason that Yaichiro favors
the Nanzenjis is Gyokuran.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:44.160
He wanted to look good
by bringing back tanuki shogi.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.120
He wants to be told, "Yaichiro-san,
you're so wonderful!"

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.900
Come on, everyone.

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:51.330
Isn't there a problem here?

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.960
Isn't this what they call
mixing business with pleasure?

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.610
I think that's rather impure,

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:00.220
and disqualifies him from
being the next Trick Magister.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:04.220
Yaichiro?

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:08.570
I was so busy playing shogi

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.950
that I missed out on my chance
at getting married.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:12.430
Yaichiro-san,

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:14.980
I beg of you, please take me as your wife.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.670
Huh?

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:26.570
Ow... or not.

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:27.570
Nii-san...

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:41.220
Sneak, sneak, ow.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:44.390
Take that!

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.520
I'm sorry, Gyokuran!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.980
I might've said a bit too much.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.990
<b>Kyoto Zoo</b>

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.990
<b>Nanzenji</b>

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.000
I told you not to get provoked by them!

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:15.130
You basically caused the Nanzenjis
trouble because of that.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:17.960
Well, those two are the ones
to blame for all this.

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:21.170
I told you to think about where
to pick a fight with them.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:25.970
Why couldn't you just say something
back at Kinkaku and Ginkaku?

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:29.180
You're the reason why
Gyokuran got embarrassed.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:33.060
Were you born just to trouble me?!

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:39.370
I've been deeply hurt.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:46.160
I'm not coming down
until you grovel, Yaichiro.

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:53.810
That's...

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.980
This must be Yaichiro's hiding spot.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.230
How boring...

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:04.960
This is...

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:07.360
Father's shogi board.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:22.970
Hm?

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:28.660
Huh...

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:30.860
The tables have turned.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:34.070
I wonder why Gyokuran moved there.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.090
I concede.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:54.180
Yaichiro sure did something really immature.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:14:00.090
Though I guess he was just a kid back then.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.660
I got some delicious yokan,
so I brought you some.

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:12.290
Your mother has taken a liking to Gyokuran.

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.960
Well, Gyokuran-sensei is a fine tanuki.

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:19.540
Let's make her Yaichiro's wife.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.460
Your mother has made up her mind.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:26.840
Well, that's rather sudden, Mother.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.890
I'm pretty sure there's some interest there.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.410
You mean the red fur of fate?

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:39.230
But it's rather difficult.
Yaichiro isn't one to play the game of love,

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:42.060
and Gyokuran seems rather shy.

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:47.760
But Yaichiro has a very kind younger brother,

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:50.490
so I'm sure that he'll
work something out for him.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.660
After all, he's {/i1}such{/i0} a kind brother,

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.970
that I'm sure he feels bad

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:59.690
about the trouble he caused
at the shogi tournament.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:00.500
Er, Mother—

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:03.190
I'm sure he'll do his best
to make it up to him.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:04.630
I just know it.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.130
Yes, indeed.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.050
Your mother understands.

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:10.820
The yokan was delicious, wasn't it?

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.140
It's premium yokan.

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.350
Yasaburo-kun.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:25.590
How's Gyokuran doing?

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:28.230
She's pretty much holed herself up.

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:30.960
When she makes up her mind to hide,

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.320
she won't listen to me at all.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:38.200
I'm sorry for all the trouble I've caused.

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:40.000
Don't worry about it.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.670
Sometimes, adversity strengthens foundations.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.460
My brother is just very clumsy
when it comes to certain things.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:50.710
Well, we are tanuki, after all.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:55.600
I understand Yaichiro very well,

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:59.980
but since his father
was such a well-renowned tanuki,

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:03.000
I'm sure that he must've felt
as though he was being watched

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.520
and made mistakes when
they usually wouldn't happen.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:10.170
When you go with the flow
and do things carefree,

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:13.030
you don't usually make huge mistakes,

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:16.110
but when you're trying
all the time to impress,

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:19.080
I think you're destined to mess up.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.600
Isn't that what tanuki are like?

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:25.220
That might be true.

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:28.350
Tanuki are known for their softness.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:32.030
But I'm very fond of Yaichiro.

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:37.340
The God of Shogi...

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.220
Huh?

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.960
We Nanzenjis say that those

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:44.010
who were drawn to and possessed by shogi

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:48.230
and then disappeared from this world
were taken away by the God of Shogi.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.190
I was worried that

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:55.740
the God of Shogi would
one day take Gyokuran, too.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.830
I always hoped that someone

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.370
would prevent it.

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:04.240
Say, Yasaburo-kun.

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:08.000
I'm actually hoping that
that someone is Yaichiro.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.840
Are you sure he'd suffice?

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.460
Of course.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:15.100
He's the one that my little sister picked.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.660
Don't talk to me right now, Yasaburo-chan.

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:25.310
I'm in the middle of reflecting.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:29.690
Isn't your behind starting
to hurt right about now?

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.700
Letting your behind get cold
will get you sick.

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:39.910
This isn't a mere pawn,

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:43.950
it is the Fool Hermit who does as he pleases.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.710
And over here, we have

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:51.340
the sly old dog, the Pink Tanuki.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:59.230
Oh, come on, Yasaburo-chan.

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:01.050
We can't really call this shogi.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:03.400
Is it that bad?

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:06.850
It feels like all your pieces are laughing.

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:10.900
I wonder if when a fool plays them,
the pieces become fools as well.

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:14.080
I'm just going to keep
playing this fool's shogi

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.130
until you agree to come down, Gyokuran.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:19.070
Oh, come on. I'm going to die from laughter.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.190
Then you should come down.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:23.490
Everyone's worried about you.

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:30.820
It appears that the tables have turned.

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:35.930
Do you remember when you were left hanging
on the giant cedar in Kumogahata?

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:38.210
You mean when Akadama-sensei 
tied me up there,

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:40.040
forgot about me, and went home, right?

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:44.610
Back then, you said you weren't
going to come down, no matter what.

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:45.770
Did I?

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:47.190
Yes.

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.490
I still remember it as clear as day.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:53.730
The sun went down,
and we still couldn't find you.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:56.320
Yaichiro-san was so worried
that I went with him

00:18:57.080 --> 00:19:00.150
to look for you in Kumogahata.

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:06.570
So, what are you going to do, Gyokuran?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.400
Are you going to stay stubborn?

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:16.360
I think I've had enough fool's shogi.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:19.840
Nii-sama.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:22.320
I'm back.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:25.970
Welcome back.

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:29.750
I'm going to head over to Tadasu Forest.

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:30.890
Is that all right?

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:33.530
Of course.

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:34.510
Go right ahead.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.460
How dare you—

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.780
If you want it back, apologize to me.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.790
What am I supposed to apologize for?

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.810
If you have no intention of apologizing,

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:52.630
We'll have to settle this in shogi.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:54.420
If I lose, I'll give it back.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:57.200
All right.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:19.980
What are you doing here, Gyokuran?

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:22.100
What happened to Yasaburo?

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:26.070
Yasaburo-chan has made a strategic retreat.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.520
Curse him.

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:29.520
What is he thinking?

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:32.250
I'm sorry for troubling you.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.790
It's fine. Let's just play shogi.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.670
Anything but that.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:40.040
Why won't you play with me?

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:44.880
I don't want to make a fool of myself again.

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:49.140
I'll never lose to you purposely again.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:52.430
I want to play shogi
with you, Yaichiro-san.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:00.920
If you would.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:08.060
<i>There is a furry little love story here.</i>

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.900
<i>They say that when a boy tanuki
and a girl tanuki fall in love,</i>

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:14.830
<i>they are bound by the red fur of fate.</i>

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:17.540
<i>The same way the red fur of fate</i>

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.840
<i>pulled my mother from
Tanukidani Fudo to Tadasu Forest,</i>

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:24.450
<i>this time, it brought someone from Nanzenji.</i>

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:26.670
<i>Truly right now,</i>

00:21:26.670 --> 00:21:28.590
<i>a Mister Tanuki and Miss Tanuki</i>

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:32.770
<i>are deepening their relationship.</i>

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:37.620
I've lost.

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:47.990
Oh, what's this?

00:21:57.950 --> 00:21:58.940
Gyokuran?!

00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:32.410
Nii-san, it's time again.

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:33.770
The Gozan Farewell Bonfire!

00:23:33.770 --> 00:23:35.100
This year we'll have...

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:37.770
...our comeback attack!

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:38.790
Hold it.

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Episode Five
 Daimonji Luxury Liner Battle Continued</b>

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:39.860
Nii-san?!
